# Copy to .env.stripe-setup AT THE REPO ROOT (not here). That path is gitignored.
#
#   cp tools/stripe-setup.env.example .env.stripe-setup
#
# Named the way tools/email-setup.env.example is, and for the same reason: the repo
# gitignores `.env*`, which would swallow the template too, and would make a file full of
# real keys look tracked-and-safe when it is merely invisible.

# --- Stripe -----------------------------------------------------------------
# A SANDBOX secret key: https://dashboard.stripe.com/sandboxes
#
# sk_test_ ONLY. The script refuses anything else at preflight, and so does
# apps/web/src/server/billing/config.ts, which returns null for a live key and therefore
# switches billing OFF rather than on. CLAUDE.md's rule is that nothing takes real money
# before the independent security review; those two checks are how that is enforced rather
# than remembered.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...

# --- Site -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only used for the WEBHOOK URL and the portal's return URL, both of which must be fixed
# public addresses Stripe can reach. The checkout and portal routes derive their origin
# from the request instead, so a preview deployment sends a preview user back to the
# preview rather than to production.
#
# For local webhook testing you do not set this to localhost. Use the Stripe CLI, which
# forwards to your machine and prints its own signing secret:
#
#   stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/billing/webhook
#
SITE_URL=https://cloakcal.com
